<title>CANADA: Canada June department store sales rise on month.</title>
<headline>Canada June department store sales rise on month.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian department stores sales rose a seasonally adjusted 0.4 percent in June from May to C$1.32 billion, Statistics Canada said on Monday.</p>
<p>In unadjusted data, year-over-year sales in June rose 9.3 percent to C$1.25 billion.</p>
<p>Sales for the first half of 1997 totalled C$7.75 billion, up 9.5 percent from a year earlier. First quarter sales were 8.7 percent and second quarter sales 10.2 percent.</p>
<p>(For more information from Statistics Canada, contact Statistics Canada, Louise Genereux, Retail Trade Section, 613-951-3549.)</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau, 613-235-6745))</p>
